  {
    "id": "47048fea4f371182b968",
    "source": "The server throws and keeps a player's six 4d6 totals. Choose whether they may throw again: never, only when the six add up to less than a total you set (70 is the default; the book names no rule), or as often as they like. This is the rule in the library and at every table that follows the server, where a player has one six for all of them. A table can set its own rule in its settings and then keeps a separate six for each player; a character made there still joins its player's library like any other, and a library character or a file brought to a table is only checked against what the dice could give.",
    "sourceHash": "47048fea4f371182b9688f74f73333cb76718680f3ada835805a992957b716d9",
